  "sections": [
    {
      "title": "When it's urgent",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "kotak",
          "title": "Six emergency sentences — learn them by heart",
          "items": [
            "**დამეხმარეთ!** (damekhmaret) — Help me!",
            "**სასწრაფო გამოიძახეთ!** (sasts'rapo gamoidzakhet) — Call an ambulance!",
            "**ცუდად ვარ.** (tsudad var) — I feel unwell / I'm about to faint.",
            "**ალერგია მაქვს.** — I have an allergy.",
            "**ინგლისურად ლაპარაკობთ?** — Do you speak English?",
            "**ინდონეზიის საელჩო.** (Indoneziis saelcho) — The Indonesian Embassy. (swap in your own country's name)"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "p",
          "text": "Two practical things best prepared before you need them. First, **112** is the only emergency number you need to remember in Georgia, and its operators speak English. Second, write your allergies and regular medicines on a slip of paper in simple Georgian — *ალერგია მაქვს …-ზე* — and keep it in your wallet. In a panic, even the simplest sentence is hard to get out."
        },
