        {
          "type": "p",
          "text": "One habit that may surprise you: Georgians ask *როგორ ხარ?* and really mean it, and if you're sick they genuinely want to know. Answering *ცოტა ავად ვარ* (I'm a bit sick) will almost certainly bring offers of medicine, tea, or a ride to the doctor from someone you met a week ago. It's not just politeness, and turning all of it down only confuses them."
